# MAP: every file on G7 that Git describes, and where it lives on each side.
# Read by g7-drift (Phase 1: compare and report) and, later, g7-apply (Phase 2: apply "yes" lines).
#
#   file  <repo>:<path>  <path on G7>  <owner:group or ->  <mode or ->  <apply yes|no>  [flags]
#   twin  <repo>:<path>  <repo>:<path>     two copies in Git that must stay identical
#   job   <Jenkins job>  <repo>:<path>     inline pipeline that must match this file
#   job-scm <Jenkins job> <script path>    pipeline read from the job's own repository
#   ignore <path on G7>                    a file on G7 that is deliberately not in Git
#
# repo: g7-infra (main) or TaxGlasses (master), both in /srv/git/repos on G7.
#   ignore-glob <pattern>                  files on G7 that belong to another repository (fnmatch)
#   ignore-job <pattern>                   Jenkins jobs that belong to another repository (any case)
#
# MemeSniper is not described here: its files on G7 are in the memesniper-deploy repository
# (g7/) and are Codex's. g7-drift never reads them (PROTECTED in the script).
# owner or mode "-": not checked yet; the report prints what G7 has, so it can be filled in.
# apply "no": checked only, never applied from Git (lock-out risk, a secret, the deploy's own
# files). Flags: redact-wg, redact-hostapd, redact-jenkins-secret (the live copy is
# redacted the same way before comparing), live-caddy (only checks it names blue or green),
# taxglasses-deploy (g7-apply waits for no deploy to be running).

